{
  "case_id": "2008-08-681",
  "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ca0a58fa4da-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 1:00 p.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ca0a58fa4da-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, Congress used different words to describe these different forms of relief, \"stay\" in (b)(3)(B) and \"enjoin\" in (f)(2). Congress used different words because it saw these forms of relief as different."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ca0a58fa4da-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Counsel, I'm not sure this matters very much, But do you know if -- are stays usually granted in this type of case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ca0a58fa4da-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: That wouldn't be deciding it the same way twice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ca0a58fa4da-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, Your Honor, the government has stated in its brief that it believes these two standards to be virtually identical."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ca0a58fa4da-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: So you think references to equitable relief and restrain are clear enough to cover the Court's authority to grant a stay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ca0a58fa4da-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Just to refresh my recollection, what -- what is the major difference between the standards that -- or the findings that the judge must make, (a) to grant a preliminary injunction and (b) to grant a stay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ca0a58fa4da-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I -- so how is it supposed to work?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Kneedler",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ca0a58fa4da-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, the Court granted the stay in connection with the -- with the granting of -- of certiorari in my case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ca0a58fa4da-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask just a technical point?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Harrison",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ca0a58fa4da-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government contends that this Court or any court of appeals could impose a stay to consider the stay motion. And, respectfully, I don't believe that is consistent with the text of (f)(2)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ca0a58fa4da-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You wouldn't apply, or would you, the same standard that you would apply on Monday for the next -- on Monday for the next year and a half?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ca0a58fa4da-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress didn't use the word \"stay\" it (f)(2). It used the word \"enjoin.\" And the fact that that word choice was different from the word it used in (b)(3)(B) I think is a clear indication that Congress had something different. It didn't cross-reference stay and didn't use the word \"stays,\" and it articulated a standard that seems more appropriate for district courts adjudicating permanent injunctive relief than courts of appeals hearing a temporary application for a stay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4ca0a58fa4da8a3b2c7de1cf7823f24e7e33796816a5ad875eb05a34c3e8740d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4ca0a58fa4da-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I just ask this one real quick: Do you understand -- is your understanding that the government's interpretation of the statute that our stay in this case violated the statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-08-681",
      "confidence": 0.0,
